    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on an audit for this new fintech app we're launching. can you give me a quick checklist of the main WCAG 2.1 requirements i should be looking for regarding color contrast and screen reader compatibility? i want to make sure we don't miss anything critical before the handoff.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For color contrast, focus on meeting WCAG AA standards, targeting a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text. Regarding screen reader compatibility, ensure all interactive elements have proper ARIA labels and that the document structure uses correct semantic HTML tags (like headings). Checking keyboard navigation is also vital, as users without screen readers rely heavily on tab order.",
      "source": "target",
